Production Issue: Ansible Deployment Broke Nginx on All Servers

Recently during a production deployment using Ansible, we pushed an update to Nginx configuration across multiple servers.

Playbook executed successfully ✅.
No errors ❌
But suddenly…

🌐 Website went down on all production servers.

HTTP 502 Bad Gateway.

🔍 What happened?

The new Nginx config file had a small syntax mistake.
Since Ansible pushed the config to all servers at once, the broken configuration was deployed everywhere.

And we did NOT validate the config before restart. 🤦‍♂️

💥 Root Cause:

We restarted Nginx without testing configuration using:

nginx -t

💡 Immediate Fix:

Logged into one server

Corrected the configuration

Tested using nginx -t

Updated playbook to include validation step before restart

✅ Permanent Fix Implemented:

- name: Validate nginx config
 command: nginx -t
 notify: Restart nginx

Now Nginx only restarts if config validation passes.

🔑 Lesson Learned:

Automation in production without validation is dangerous.

Just because Ansible shows "SUCCESS"
Doesn’t mean your application is healthy.

DevOps is not just automation.
It’s safe automation.

